  "foaf:name": "Ocean Data Liberation Project",
  "sdo:name": "Ocean Data Liberation Project",
  "sdo:description": "DeepOcean is advancing a data liberation project with Akvaplan niva and the UK Met Office, addressing Ocean Decade Challenges 7 and 8. The project promotes collaboration to improve ocean models, reuses non-sensitive commercial data, and enhances ocean condition predictions. Data liberation refers to making previously stored data accessible for scientific use, reducing the need for new data collection and associated emissions. This aims to make an increased quantity of data available to the scientific community to aid understanding of physical oceanographic and meteorological processes. ROV-collected CTD data is shared with the Met Office and Akvaplan niva’s ROC in Tromsø for QC and model integration, including into Norway’s Norkyst-800. The goal is to expand geographically and include more end users. Future plans include launching Akvaplan niva’s gliders from commercial vessels for long-term environmental monitoring and integrating USV Challenger CTD data into the project.",
